{"question_text": {"৪৯তম বিসিএস ⎯ ফলিত গণিত (৫৬১)": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) The stream function Ψ(x, y) represents:<br>", "option1": "The velocity potential of the fluid<br>", "option2": "Streamlines of the flow<br>", "option3": "Vorticity of the flow<br>", "option4": "Pressure distribution in the flow<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>For 2D flow, Ψ is constant along a streamline.<br>The curves Ψ = constant represent streamlines.</p>"}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) In 2D Cartesian flow (x, y), the velocity components (u, v) in terms of the stream function ψ are:<br>", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_lYKoLKS.png\" width=\"234\" height=\"59\"><br>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_mUFwEpB.png\" width=\"237\" height=\"47\"><br>", "option3": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip3_SUOVmFN.png\" width=\"252\" height=\"55\"><br>", "option4": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip4_c5Q7ryv.png\" width=\"269\" height=\"50\"><br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Definition of stream function ensures incompressibility: ∇·q = 0.<br>Relation: u = ∂Ψ∂y, v = −∂Ψ/∂x</p>"}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) For 2D polar flow (r, θ), the velocity components (q<sub>r</sub>, q<sub>θ</sub>) in terms of stream function Ψ(r, θ) are<br>", "option1": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_XqZHF4j.png\" width=\"399\" height=\"67\"><br>", "option2": "<img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_azt1amn.png\" width=\"421\" height=\"63\"><br>", "option3": "q<sub>r​ </sub>= ∂Ψ/∂r, q<sub>θ </sub>= ∂Ψ/∂θ<br>", "option4": "qr​ = ∂Ψ/∂θ, qθ ​= - ∂Ψ/∂r<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_ZnSvb6x.png\" width=\"413\" height=\"135\"></p>"}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) The stream function of a 2D flow is:<br>Ψ = xy Find the velocity components (u, v).<br>", "option1": "u = y, v = - x<br>", "option2": "u = - y, v = x<br>", "option3": "u = - x, v = y<br>", "option4": "u = x, v = - y<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p>u = ∂Ψ/∂y = ∂(xy)/∂y = x, v= −∂Ψ/∂x = −∂(xy)/∂x = −y</p>"}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) Stream function: Ψ = r<sup>2</sup>sin⁡θ<br>Compute q<sub>r </sub>and q<sub>θ</sub>​  at r=1, θ = π/2.<br>", "option1": "q<sub>r </sub>​= - 1, q<sub>θ ​</sub>= - 2<br>", "option2": "q<sub>r​ </sub>= 1, q<sub>θ </sub>​=2<br>", "option3": "q<sub>r​ </sub>= - 1, q<sub>θ</sub>​ = 2<br>", "option4": "None of these<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_D5IlBaj.png\" width=\"686\" height=\"112\"></p>"}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) Stream function: Ψ = x<sup>2 </sup>- y<sup>2<br></sup>Find the velocity components (u, v) at (x = 1, y = 2).<br>", "option1": "u= - 2, u = - 2<br>", "option2": "u = - 2, v = - 4<br>", "option3": "u = - 4, v = - 2<br>", "option4": "u = 4, v = 2<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_yB1FrFz.png\" width=\"617\" height=\"90\"></p>"}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) Stream function: Ψ = x<sup>2 </sup>+ y<sup>2</sup><br>The streamlines represent-<br>", "option1": "Circles around the origin<br>", "option2": "Straight lines along x-axis<br>", "option3": "Straight lines along y-axis<br>", "option4": "It is impossible to define<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Stream function  is constant along stream line.<br>Ψ = constant → x² + y² = constant → circles around origin</p>"}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) Stream function:<br>Ψ = rsin⁡θ Find radial velocity at r = 2,θ = π/2.<br>", "option1": "0<br>", "option2": "1<br>", "option3": "2<br>", "option4": "- 1<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_km97QfH.png\"></p>"}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) For 2D flow: Ψ = xy <br>Compute the velocity magnitude at (x = 2, y = 1).<br>", "option1": "2<br>", "option2": "3<br>", "option3": "√5<br>", "option4": "0<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_IJ1YmEu.png\"></p>"}, {"id": "10", "question": "১০) Why does the use of stream function automatically satisfy the continuity equation in 2D incompressible flow?<br>", "option1": "Because velocity is always constant<br>", "option2": "Because ∂u/∂x​ + ∂v/∂y ​= 0 holds identically<br>", "option3": "Because flow is always steady<br>", "option4": "Because pressure gradient is zero<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_IeYTvoN.png\" width=\"556\" height=\"147\"></p>"}, {"id": "11", "question": "১১) If a velocity field has a stream function Ψ\\psiΨ, does it guarantee irrotational flow?<br>", "option1": "Yes, always<br>", "option2": "No, stream function only ensures continuity<br>", "option3": "Yes, if pressure is constant<br>", "option4": "Only in potential flow<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>A stream function ensures continuity in 2D incompressible flow, but irrotationality requires ∇ × q = 0.</p>"}, {"id": "12", "question": "১২) For Ψ = 2, what does the curve represent?<br>", "option1": "A pathline<br>", "option2": "A streamline<br>", "option3": "A velocity potential line<br>", "option4": "None of these<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>Ψ = const is always a streamline.</p>"}, {"id": "13", "question": "১৩) If both a stream function Ψ and a velocity potential φ exist for a 2D flow, the flow must be:<br>", "option1": "Only incompressible<br>", "option2": "Only irrotational<br>", "option3": "Incompressible and irrotational<br>", "option4": "Steady but rotational<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>Stream function Ψ → continuity satisfied (incompressible)<br>Velocity potential φ → irrotational condition satisfied.<br>So both together ⇒ incompressible &amp; irrotational.</p>"}, {"id": "14", "question": "১৪) If Ψ and φ exist simultaneously, which condition holds?<br>", "option1": "∂Ψ/∂x​ = ∂φ/∂y​, ∂Ψ/∂y = - ∂φ​/∂x<br>", "option2": "∂Ψ/∂x ​= ∂φ/∂y​, ∂Ψ​/∂y = ∂φ/∂x<br>", "option3": "∂Ψ/∂y​ = ∂φ/∂x​, ∂Ψ​/∂y = - ∂φ​/∂x<br>", "option4": "∂Ψ/∂y​ = ∂φ/∂x​, ∂Ψ​/∂y = ∂φ​/∂x<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>These are the Cauchy–Riemann equations in fluid flow form.</p>"}, {"id": "15", "question": "১৫) Given Ψ = x<sup>2 </sup>- y<sup>2</sup>, does a velocity potential φ exist?<br>", "option1": "Yes, because continuity holds<br>", "option2": "Yes, because Cauchy–Riemann equations are satisfied<br>", "option3": "No, because ∇ × q ≠ 0<br>", "option4": "No, because flow is compressible<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p>ক) Yes, because continuity holds → Continuity is necessary but not sufficient.×<br>খ) Yes, because Cauchy–Riemann equations are satisfied →  Correct √<br>গ) No, because ∇×q≠0 → vorticity is 0 ×<br>ঘ) No, because flow is compressible → the flow is incompressible ×</p>"}, {"id": "16", "question": "১৬) Given φ =x<sup>2 </sup>- y<sup>2</sup>, find the corresponding stream function Ψ. <br>", "option1": "Ψ = 2xy<br>", "option2": "Ψ = - 2xy<br>", "option3": "Ψ = x<sup>2 </sup>+ y<sup>2</sup><br>", "option4": "Ψ = ln(x<sup>2 </sup>+ y<sup>2</sup>)<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_2j8aFFe.png\" width=\"289\" height=\"58\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_ghLfNAC.png\" width=\"386\" height=\"100\"><br><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip2_rVy0w0q.png\" width=\"343\" height=\"77\"></p>"}, {"id": "17", "question": "১৭) If φ and Ψ exist, the function, w(z) = Φ + iΨ  represents-<br>", "option1": "Pressure distribution<br>", "option2": "Velocity distribution<br>", "option3": "Complex potential of flow<br>", "option4": "Lamb’s equation<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p>w(z) is the complex potential, widely used in potential flow theory.</p>"}, {"id": "18", "question": "১৮) Velocity potential in polar coordinates: φ = rcosθ Find q<sub>r​ </sub>and q<sub>θ​</sub>.<br>", "option1": "q<sub>r </sub>​= cosθ, q<sub>θ </sub>​= - sinθ<br>", "option2": "q<sub>r​ </sub>= sinθ, q<sub>θ​ </sub>= cosθ<br>", "option3": " q<sub>r</sub>​ = -cosθ, q<sub>θ </sub>​= sinθ<br>", "option4": "q<sub>r ​</sub>= r, q<sub>θ​ </sub>= 0<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_ydkyKME.png\" width=\"517\" height=\"187\"></p>"}, {"id": "19", "question": "১৯) For the same flow, φ = rcosθ, the stream function Ψ is<br>", "option1": "- rsinθ<br>", "option2": "- r<sup>2</sup>sinθ<br>", "option3": "lnr<br>", "option4": "-sinr<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>q<sub>r​ </sub>= -cosθ, q<sub>θ </sub>​= sinθ.</p>\r\n<p>Check with Ψ  =-rsinθ:</p>\r\n<p>q<sub>r ​</sub>= (1/r) ∂Ψ/∂θ = (1/r)(-rcos⁡θ) = -cos⁡θ, <br>q<sub>θ </sub>= -∂Ψ /∂r = sin⁡θ<br>Matches the velocity field.</p>"}, {"id": "20", "question": "২০) Stream function: Ψ = r<sup>2</sup>cos⁡θ<br>Find q<sub>r </sub>at r = 2,  θ = π/3.<br>", "option1": "0<br>", "option2": "1<br>", "option3": "- √3<br>", "option4": "- 1<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_AzR6evY.png\" width=\"633\" height=\"182\"></p>"}, {"id": "21", "question": "২১) Given stream function, Ψ = x<sup>2</sup>y - y<sup>3<br></sup>Find (u,v) and check whether the flow is rotational or irrotational.<br>", "option1": "u = x<sup>2</sup>−3y<sup>2</sup>, v = −2xy, rotational<br>", "option2": "u = x<sup>2</sup>−3y<sup>2</sup>, v = −2xy, irrotational<br>", "option3": "u = 2xy, v = 3y<sup>2</sup>−x<sup>2</sup>, rotational<br>", "option4": "u = 2xy, v = 3y<sup>2</sup>−x<sup>2</sup>, irrotational<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_3KQpUFt.png\" width=\"504\" height=\"198\"></p>"}, {"id": "22", "question": "২২) Given stream function, Ψ = x<sup>2</sup>y<br>Check if a velocity potential exists.<br>", "option1": "Yes, φ = x<sup>2</sup>y<br>", "option2": "Yes, φ = x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup><br>", "option3": "Yes, φ = -2xy<br>", "option4": "No velocity potential exists<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_hKua79Z.png\" width=\"505\" height=\"245\"></p>"}, {"id": "23", "question": "২৩) Stream function, Ψ = r<sup>3</sup>sin⁡θ​ <br>Find transverse velocity at r = 1,  θ = π/4.<br>", "option1": "3/√2<br>", "option2": "-3/√2<br>", "option3": "1/√2<br>", "option4": "-1/√2<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_4pbhyrr.png\" width=\"575\" height=\"328\"></p>"}, {"id": "24", "question": "২৪) For the stream function, Ψ = y<sup>3</sup> <br>Determine the nature of the flow<br>", "option1": "Rotational, velocity potential exists<br>", "option2": "Rotational, no velocity potential exists<br>", "option3": "Uniform flow<br>", "option4": "Irrotational, velocity potential exists<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_QrDTTxD.png\" width=\"519\" height=\"227\"></p>"}, {"id": "25", "question": "২৫) Given stream function, Ψ = x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2<br></sup>Check if velocity potential φ\\phiφ exists.<br>", "option1": "Yes, φ = x<sup>2</sup>y<sup>2</sup><br>", "option2": "Yes, φ = x<sup>3</sup>−y<sup>3</sup><br>", "option3": "Yes, φ = 2xy<br>", "option4": "No velocity potential exists<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_OUwrP0A.png\" width=\"481\" height=\"275\"></p>"}, {"id": "26", "question": "২৬) For the velocity field, u = 2x, v = −2y<br>Identify the type of flow.<br>", "option1": "Uniform flow<br>", "option2": "Rotational flow<br>", "option3": "Pure strain (extensional flow)<br>", "option4": "Doublet flow<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_mFAMbe7.png\" width=\"490\" height=\"134\"><br><br>Flow is irrotational but velocities vary with position → this is a pure extensional (strain) flow.</p>"}, {"id": "27", "question": "২৭) If φ = x<sup>3 </sup>- 3xy<sup>2 </sup>then velocity components are-<br>", "option1": "u = 3x<sup>2 </sup>- 3y<sup>2</sup>, v = − 6xy<br>", "option2": "u = 3x<sup>2 </sup>+ 3y<sup>2</sup>, v = - 6xy<br>", "option3": "u = 2x, v = - 2y<br>", "option4": "u = - 3x<sup>2 </sup>+ 3y<sup>2</sup>,  v = 6xy<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_2Yrvox7.png\" width=\"576\" height=\"187\"></p>"}, {"id": "28", "question": "২৮) For Ψ = r<sup>2</sup>sin(2θ) then find q<sub>θ</sub><br>", "option1": "−2rsin(2θ)<br>", "option2": "2rsin(2θ)<br>", "option3": "−2r<sup>2</sup>cos(2θ)<br>", "option4": "2r<sup>2</sup>cos(2θ)<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_q5kODO7.png\" width=\"402\" height=\"116\"></p>"}, {"id": "29", "question": "২৯) Stream function Ψ = sin(x)sin(y) then find (u, v).<br>", "option1": "u = sin(x)sin(y), v = −cos(x)cos(y)<br>", "option2": "u = cos(x)sin(y), v = −sin(x)cos(y)<br>", "option3": "u = cos(x)cos(y), v = −sin(x)sin(y)<br>", "option4": "u = sin(x)cos(y), v = −cos(x)sin(y)<br>", "answer": "4", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_Y4O1FeF.png\" width=\"775\" height=\"89\"></p>"}, {"id": "30", "question": "৩০) φ = ln(r), Find q<sub>r​</sub> in polar coordinates.<br>", "option1": "1/r<br>", "option2": "r<br>", "option3": "-1/r<br>", "option4": "0<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_6tWz3KI.png\" width=\"366\" height=\"126\"></p>"}, {"id": "31", "question": "৩১) A flow has velocity components u = y, v = x.<br>Which of the following statements is correct?<br>", "option1": "Flow is rotational and velocity potential exists<br>", "option2": "Flow is irrotational and velocity potential exists<br>", "option3": "Flow is rotational and velocity potential does not exist<br>", "option4": "Flow is irrotational but velocity potential does not exist<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_R6H4unM.png\" width=\"505\" height=\"95\"><br><br>Flow is irrotational → velocity potential exists.</p>"}, {"id": "32", "question": "৩২) The difference in stream function values between two streamlines in 2D incompressible flow represents:<br>", "option1": "<span>Pressure difference</span><br>", "option2": "Velocity magnitude difference<br>", "option3": "Volumetric flow rate per unit depth between the streamlines<br>", "option4": "Vorticity<br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><span>In 2D incompressible flow, </span><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Δ</mi><mi>ψ</mi><mo>=</mo><mtext>flow rate per unit depth</mtext></mrow></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mord\">ΔΨ </span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span><span class=\"mspace\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">flow rate per unit depth</span></span></span></span></span><span> between two streamlines.</span></p>"}, {"id": "33", "question": "৩৩) For Ψ = x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup>, the flow is<br>", "option1": "Rotational with constant vorticity<br>", "option2": "Irrotational<br>", "option3": "Uniform flow<br>", "option4": "Potential flow only in polar coordinates<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_sDYTEQq.png\" width=\"1205\" height=\"68\"></p>"}, {"id": "34", "question": "৩৪) If Ψ = y<sup>2</sup>, the flow rate per unit depth between y = 1 and y = 3 is:<br>", "option1": "6<br>", "option2": "8<br>", "option3": "9<br>", "option4": "4<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_1JEq0OA.png\" width=\"412\" height=\"36\"></p>"}, {"id": "35", "question": "৩৫) The condition for existence of a 2D stream function is:<br>", "option1": "<span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">(∂u</span><span class=\"mord\">/∂</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">x) </span><span class=\"mspace\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+ (∂</span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">v</span><span class=\"mord\">/∂</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">y) </span><span class=\"mspace\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">= </span><span class=\"mspace\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span><br>", "option2": "(∂u/∂y) - (∂v/∂x) = 0<br>", "option3": "∂u/∂x = ∂v/∂y<br>", "option4": "(∂u/∂y) + (∂v/∂x) = 0<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p>Continuity condition for incompressible flow.</p>"}, {"id": "36", "question": "৩৬) In irrotational 2D flow, streamlines and equipotential lines are:<br>", "option1": "<span>Always perpendicular</span><br>", "option2": "Always parallel<br>", "option3": "Identical<br>", "option4": "Never related<br>", "answer": "1", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_yV7d0Xm.png\" width=\"616\" height=\"384\"></p>"}, {"id": "37", "question": "৩৭) The velocity potential is:<br>Φ(r, θ) = r<sup>2</sup>cos2θ<br>Find q<sub>r​</sub> and q<sub>θ</sub>​ at r=1,θ = π/4.<br>", "option1": "-1 &amp; 2 respectively<br>", "option2": "0 &amp; 2<br>", "option3": "-2 &amp; 2<br>", "option4": "-1 &amp; 2<br>", "answer": "2", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_k3xpVg7.png\" width=\"472\" height=\"47\"><br><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip1_o9PsF2s.png\" width=\"471\" height=\"54\"></p>"}, {"id": "38", "question": "৩৮) The velocity potential for a 2D flow is Φ(x, y) = 3xy<br>Find the velocity components u and v at the point (x, y) = (2,1)<br>", "option1": "u=−6, v=−3 <br>", "option2": "u=6, v=3 <br>", "option3": "u=−3, v=−6 <br>", "option4": "u=3, v=6 <br>", "answer": "3", "exp": "<p><img src=\"https://elasticbeanstalk-ap-southeast-1-051040323559.s3.amazonaws.com/livemcq-files/media/uploads/mceclip0_qGeBk0I.png\" width=\"236\" height=\"1